WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.699
(fast shamisen music)

00:00:03.699 --> 00:00:05.650
- [Narrator] The shamisen
is one of Japan's

00:00:05.650 --> 00:00:08.131
traditional musical instruments.

00:00:08.131 --> 00:00:09.798
Among its performers,

00:00:09.798 --> 00:00:14.646
the Yoshida brothers are
known to play a quick tempo.

00:00:14.646 --> 00:00:16.063
Lightening quick.

00:00:17.700 --> 00:00:20.783
(audicence clapping)

00:00:22.786 --> 00:00:25.536
(shamisen music)

00:00:33.869 --> 00:00:37.022
The Yoshida brothers are
masters of the shamisen,

00:00:37.022 --> 00:00:39.605
a classic Japanese guitar famous for being

00:00:39.605 --> 00:00:42.926
the accompanying music in
Japanese kabuki theater.

00:00:42.926 --> 00:00:45.835
But the shamisen has various genres

00:00:45.835 --> 00:00:48.918
and has evolved from an ancient past.

00:01:11.835 --> 00:01:13.635
The brothers began learning the shamisen

00:01:13.635 --> 00:01:15.656
at just 5 years old.

00:01:15.656 --> 00:01:16.675
As they progressed,

00:01:16.675 --> 00:01:19.915
they fell in love with the
genre of tsugaru-shamisen,

00:01:19.915 --> 00:01:21.990
which is over 150 years old

00:01:21.990 --> 00:01:24.240
and has a very quick tempo.

00:01:48.212 --> 00:01:50.093
The brothers have revitalized the shamisen

00:01:50.093 --> 00:01:53.375
for audiences today by
melding new modern sounds

00:01:53.375 --> 00:01:54.914
with the ancient art.

00:01:54.914 --> 00:01:56.274
And in doing so,

00:01:56.274 --> 00:01:58.981
they've gained popularity worldwide.

00:01:58.981 --> 00:02:02.732
(audience clapping)

00:02:02.732 --> 00:02:06.252
They perform to sold-out concert
halls throughout the year

00:02:06.252 --> 00:02:09.202
in the hopes of spreading
their love for their craft.

00:02:09.202 --> 00:02:10.641
But the intensity of their playing

00:02:10.641 --> 00:02:13.058
takes a toll on their bodies.

00:02:44.361 --> 00:02:47.361
(audience clapping)

